WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:03.294
(swooshes)

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:05.032
- Failure is a stepping stone to success.

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:06.629
- Fail your way to success.

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:07.462
- Failure.

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:09.111
- Failure is a part of
the learning process.

00:00:09.111 --> 00:00:11.721
- Success is moving from
one failure to the next.

00:00:11.721 --> 00:00:13.598
- To get past your failure, you've got

00:00:13.598 --> 00:00:15.457
to go through the failure.

00:00:15.457 --> 00:00:18.169
- Success is merely the
hangover of failure.

00:00:18.169 --> 00:00:19.843
- You should seek failures.

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:21.730
- Learn from those
mistakes, and get smarter.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.512
- Hello, Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:24.512 --> 00:00:26.630
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.493
that entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:30.773
all the major problems of the world.

00:00:30.773 --> 00:00:32.438
So to help you on your journey, today,

00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:36.381
we're going to learn how you
can turn failure into success.

00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:38.053
And as always, guys, if you hear something

00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:39.422
that really resonates with you,

00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:41.126
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:41.126 --> 00:00:42.677
Put quotes around it, so other people

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:45.583
can be inspired as well,
and when you write it down,

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:48.423
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself, too.

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:49.656
Enjoy.

00:00:49.656 --> 00:00:52.906
(bright hopeful music)

00:01:01.223 --> 00:01:02.852
- Failure is part of life.

00:01:02.852 --> 00:01:03.685
- Yeah.

00:01:03.685 --> 00:01:05.015
- I mean, the difference for me, though,

00:01:05.015 --> 00:01:07.174
I look at failure as a
stepping stone to success.

00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:08.197
It's a speed bump.

00:01:08.197 --> 00:01:11.318
I know I'm going to fail,
but it's not failure

00:01:11.318 --> 00:01:13.461
if you learn something, and so, gosh,

00:01:13.461 --> 00:01:14.821
I've made so many mistakes.

00:01:14.821 --> 00:01:16.075
I've screwed so many things up,

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.022
but every time I do, it just becomes,

00:01:19.022 --> 00:01:21.603
it becomes a way for me
to explain to someone else

00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:23.003
what it takes, you know.

00:01:23.003 --> 00:01:24.465
It's like, here's what I've done.

00:01:24.465 --> 00:01:26.595
I think I have the ability
to influence people

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:28.215
because I like, talk about my failures.

00:01:28.215 --> 00:01:30.790
I talk about all the
things that mess me up,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.448
but I show people I didn't let it stop me,

00:01:32.448 --> 00:01:33.626
and you don't need to let it stop you.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.597
I think that's really
the secret in that area.

00:01:35.597 --> 00:01:37.143
- And if everything you
touched was successful,

00:01:37.143 --> 00:01:39.220
you probably wouldn't be able
to relate to people as much.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.219
- No, you wouldn't be able to relate,

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:41.142
and also, it'd be total bull--

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:41.975
- Right.

00:01:41.975 --> 00:01:42.945
- And everyone will know it's bull,

00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:44.316
and also you'd be bored silly.

00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:45.149
- Right.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:45.982
- I mean, think about it.

00:01:45.982 --> 00:01:47.190
If you just said, I want
this, and it happened.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.023
I want this, and it happened.

00:01:48.023 --> 00:01:51.548
You know, people don't value
what they don't fight for.

00:01:51.548 --> 00:01:53.457
You know, it's like
you see kids sometimes.

00:01:53.457 --> 00:01:54.968
You know, your parent's will say,

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.212
you're not going to value
this if you don't work for it.

00:01:56.212 --> 00:01:57.853
And you're kid's goin', I'll value it.

00:01:57.853 --> 00:01:58.971
Just give it to me.

00:01:58.971 --> 00:01:59.804
(laughs)

00:01:59.804 --> 00:02:00.637
It's true.

00:02:00.637 --> 00:02:01.617
- Yeah.

00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:02.784
- You know, about things
we we work the hardest for,

00:02:02.784 --> 00:02:05.384
we value the most, so I think, you know,

00:02:05.384 --> 00:02:07.997
the purpose of the goal's
not getting it anyway.

00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:10.014
The purpose of the goal,
you know, is who you become.

00:02:10.014 --> 00:02:11.894
Who you become is going to make you happy

00:02:11.894 --> 00:02:13.004
or is going to make you sad.

00:02:13.004 --> 00:02:13.837
- Yeah.

00:02:13.837 --> 00:02:15.892
- So I'm not looking for
an effortless approach.

00:02:15.892 --> 00:02:16.888
- Sure, sure, sure, sure.

00:02:16.888 --> 00:02:17.844
- There's no such thing.

00:02:17.844 --> 00:02:21.232
- If you constantly remind
yourself after every defeat,

00:02:21.232 --> 00:02:24.497
after every setback, every
time you get knocked down,

00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:25.330
I've got a saying.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.661
If like knocks you down,
try and land on your back

00:02:27.661 --> 00:02:30.143
because if you look up, you can get up.

00:02:30.143 --> 00:02:32.916
See, a lot of people because
of failure, they stop.

00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:33.899
They stop believing.

00:02:33.899 --> 00:02:34.912
Let me share something with you.

00:02:34.912 --> 00:02:37.162
You will fail your way to success.

00:02:37.162 --> 00:02:38.043
Yes.

00:02:38.043 --> 00:02:40.851
Eight out of 10 millionaires
have been financially bankrupt.

00:02:40.851 --> 00:02:43.350
You will fail your way to success.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.456
It doesn't matter how many times you fail.

00:02:45.456 --> 00:02:47.466
It doesn't matter how
many times people tell you

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.830
that you can't do it.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.846
It doesn't matter if you
don't have a dime in the bank.

00:02:51.846 --> 00:02:54.020
You will fail your way to success.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.991
- I've learned more from
failures than success.

00:02:56.991 --> 00:03:01.158
And it can be paralyzing, this
failure and the fear of it.

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:05.323
My first album I made was a
album called Reasonable Doubt,

00:03:05.323 --> 00:03:09.236
which in the small circles
was considered the album,

00:03:09.236 --> 00:03:12.659
like a classic album, like
the album for that generation

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.064
and the voice of, you know, people

00:03:15.064 --> 00:03:17.322
that were going through situations.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:21.081
But it didn't sell massive
numbers worldwide, right.

00:03:21.081 --> 00:03:22.836
It was still very niche.

00:03:22.836 --> 00:03:26.005
My second album, because of,
you know, Reasonable Doubt,

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.163
and it's lack of commercial
success, you know,

00:03:29.163 --> 00:03:31.259
I try to make these
records that were bigger

00:03:31.259 --> 00:03:35.092
and will be more popular,
which was a failure.

00:03:39.848 --> 00:03:43.581
Going for that success really
messed up that project,

00:03:43.581 --> 00:03:46.058
and, you know, set a bad tone.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.408
It was a huge learning lesson for me

00:03:48.408 --> 00:03:50.136
that if I was going to be successful,

00:03:50.136 --> 00:03:51.744
I had to be successful as myself.

00:03:51.744 --> 00:03:55.079
I couldn't be successful doing
what other people were doing.

00:03:55.079 --> 00:03:59.353
I had to do what I believed
in and what felt real to me

00:03:59.353 --> 00:04:00.717
and felt true to me.

00:04:00.717 --> 00:04:03.121
- Failure is a part of the
learning process, right?

00:04:03.121 --> 00:04:04.450
What's the risk of failure?

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.324
What, you'll be embarrassed?

00:04:06.324 --> 00:04:08.194
Or risk of failure, how do you

00:04:08.194 --> 00:04:09.592
distinguish failure from learning?

00:04:09.592 --> 00:04:13.582
In your whole life, you
know, failure implies

00:04:13.582 --> 00:04:15.779
that it stops, the game stops, right?

00:04:15.779 --> 00:04:19.050
If it's part of your
failing, and then you learn,

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:23.217
then, that learning is
part of the moving forward,

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:27.438
so that is what the process is like.

00:04:27.438 --> 00:04:31.692
Fail, learn, move forward,
and constantly do that

00:04:31.692 --> 00:04:33.897
because you're cutting edge.

00:04:33.897 --> 00:04:35.198
You're going where people

00:04:35.198 --> 00:04:36.470
haven't been before in inventiveness.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.637
- If you say, I'm a fraud.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:40.856
They'll figure me out.

00:04:40.856 --> 00:04:41.994
I'll never be able to do it again.

00:04:41.994 --> 00:04:43.390
That's an artist's thought process.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.728
You're an artist.

00:04:44.728 --> 00:04:45.561
(laughs)

00:04:45.561 --> 00:04:46.591
If you're thinking like that,
you're on the right track

00:04:46.591 --> 00:04:47.628
cause they all feel that way.

00:04:47.628 --> 00:04:49.892
So there's always some
success that can come out

00:04:49.892 --> 00:04:50.898
even out of your failures.

00:04:50.898 --> 00:04:53.345
In fact, probably your
biggest successes will come

00:04:53.345 --> 00:04:54.543
directly from your failures.

00:04:54.543 --> 00:04:56.910
You should almost take that
Winston Churchill's quote

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.703
is my favorite, "Success
is moving from one

00:04:59.703 --> 00:05:01.956
"failure to the next
with great enthusiasm."

00:05:01.956 --> 00:05:04.193
You should be very enthusiastic
about your failures

00:05:04.193 --> 00:05:05.751
cause you're going to learn something.

00:05:05.751 --> 00:05:07.925
You're going to go that
way when everyone else

00:05:07.925 --> 00:05:09.931
is going that way, and
you're going to stumble,

00:05:09.931 --> 00:05:11.536
but you're also going to stumble upon

00:05:11.536 --> 00:05:12.991
something that no one else thought of.

00:05:12.991 --> 00:05:13.824
- Yeah.

00:05:13.824 --> 00:05:14.846
- You just keep going and keep going.

00:05:14.846 --> 00:05:16.924
And you're going to fail and
then rise up and fail again,

00:05:16.924 --> 00:05:17.959
and that's the journey.

00:05:17.959 --> 00:05:19.150
Up and down, man.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.180
- You don't make excuses for the failure.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.304
You grieve it.

00:05:22.304 --> 00:05:23.137
You feel the pain.

00:05:23.137 --> 00:05:24.477
You don't brush it off.

00:05:24.477 --> 00:05:26.068
You don't downplay it.

00:05:26.068 --> 00:05:30.645
You feel the pain, and you
don't rush to feel better.

00:05:30.645 --> 00:05:33.121
Now, listen, this is a principle of life

00:05:33.121 --> 00:05:35.228
I'm about to tell you.

00:05:35.228 --> 00:05:38.758
To get past it, you got to go through it.

00:05:38.758 --> 00:05:40.113
That's true in so many areas,

00:05:40.113 --> 00:05:42.807
but it's particularly true with failure.

00:05:42.807 --> 00:05:46.002
To get past your failure,
that failure in your life,

00:05:46.002 --> 00:05:47.099
you got to go through it.

00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:48.820
You cannot go around your failure.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.047
You can't go over your failure.

00:05:51.047 --> 00:05:52.924
You can't go under your failure.

00:05:52.924 --> 00:05:54.372
You can't ignore your failure.

00:05:54.372 --> 00:05:57.660
You need to grieve the failure.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.194
You need to feel the pain.

00:05:59.194 --> 00:06:02.783
Now, we don't like feeling
bad, but grief is a good thing.

00:06:02.783 --> 00:06:05.546
Grief is the way we get
through the failure,

00:06:05.546 --> 00:06:09.498
and grief is the way we learn the lessons.

00:06:09.498 --> 00:06:11.685
So often we want to just, when we fail,

00:06:11.685 --> 00:06:13.313
we want to just forget it.

00:06:13.313 --> 00:06:14.460
Push it aside.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.171
Stuff our emotions.

00:06:16.171 --> 00:06:19.345
And then, immediately
go to the next thing.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.560
When you stuff your
emotions, when you swallow

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.834
your emotions, your stomach keeps score.

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:27.248
It's kind of like, what
if you took a can of Coke,

00:06:27.248 --> 00:06:29.180
and you shook it up for a long time,

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.857
and then you put it in the freezer?

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.080
What's going to happen to it?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.671
It's going to explode eventually.

00:06:35.671 --> 00:06:37.363
It's going to come out sideways.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:40.027
And this happens in your
life when you don't deal

00:06:40.027 --> 00:06:42.223
with your emotions properly.

00:06:42.223 --> 00:06:45.017
This is why sometimes
six months after failure,

00:06:45.017 --> 00:06:46.934
a marriage falls apart.

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:51.320
Or six months after
somebody gets laid off work,

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.859
there's another problem.

00:06:52.859 --> 00:06:55.025
There's a physical health
problem, things like this,

00:06:55.025 --> 00:06:57.046
because you've shaken up the can,

00:06:57.046 --> 00:06:59.770
and you've got all these
emotions, feeling inside,

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.871
of shame and regret
and fear and insecurity

00:07:03.871 --> 00:07:05.458
and all the things that come with failure.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.807
And you're not dealing with 'em,

00:07:07.807 --> 00:07:09.318
and so you shake it up and say, we're just

00:07:09.318 --> 00:07:10.992
going to put this in the
refrigerator and try to forget

00:07:10.992 --> 00:07:12.465
about it and we're going to freeze it.

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.221
And it's going to explode, and
it's going to come out sideways

00:07:14.221 --> 00:07:16.971
in an affair or in wrong behavior

00:07:18.461 --> 00:07:20.211
or in impulsivity or in addiction

00:07:20.211 --> 00:07:22.275
or all kinds of other things.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:26.653
I've seen this thousands
of times in people's lives.

00:07:26.653 --> 00:07:28.266
You don't minimize it.

00:07:28.266 --> 00:07:29.452
You don't rush to feel better.

00:07:29.452 --> 00:07:31.218
To get past your failure, you've got to

00:07:31.218 --> 00:07:33.676
go through the failure.

00:07:33.676 --> 00:07:36.174
- You know, and my mentality is like,

00:07:36.174 --> 00:07:40.119
I have a I don't lose mentality,
and that's with anything.

00:07:40.119 --> 00:07:42.924
That's not like say, a
sporting event or whatever.

00:07:42.924 --> 00:07:46.568
That's just life, right,
because life is non-stop tests.

00:07:46.568 --> 00:07:47.841
You know what I mean?

00:07:47.841 --> 00:07:49.809
And we're always being put to the test.

00:07:49.809 --> 00:07:52.419
There's always challenges,
obstacles, et cetera,

00:07:52.419 --> 00:07:56.376
and I literally don't accept any of that

00:07:56.376 --> 00:07:58.354
as an impediment, as a negative.

00:07:58.354 --> 00:08:00.753
It's like, good, this is
going to make me stronger.

00:08:00.753 --> 00:08:02.193
I'm going to learn something from this.

00:08:02.193 --> 00:08:06.110
- I think the best advice
that I could give you

00:08:07.155 --> 00:08:09.988
on success is to know that success

00:08:11.341 --> 00:08:13.850
is merely the hangover of failure.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:18.038
And that failure is an
essential ingredient

00:08:18.038 --> 00:08:20.957
in creating a learning atmosphere for you

00:08:20.957 --> 00:08:23.641
so that you can accrue those learnings,

00:08:23.641 --> 00:08:27.056
those small incremental steps of failure

00:08:27.056 --> 00:08:29.198
and collect enough learning so that

00:08:29.198 --> 00:08:31.247
you can arrive at success, right?

00:08:31.247 --> 00:08:35.164
I think we're taught in
the system that failure

00:08:36.506 --> 00:08:39.746
is something that you
should be ashamed of.

00:08:39.746 --> 00:08:42.325
Failure is for the dumb kids

00:08:42.325 --> 00:08:45.274
cause you get an F or you get a D, right.

00:08:45.274 --> 00:08:46.290
You're not competent.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.488
You didn't comply.

00:08:47.488 --> 00:08:50.493
You didn't create the
evidence of your worthiness.

00:08:50.493 --> 00:08:53.307
But I could tell you someone
who is successful, right,

00:08:53.307 --> 00:08:56.237
both financially and
from a wealth creation

00:08:56.237 --> 00:08:58.830
point of view, but more
importantly, a wealth that matters.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:02.103
That success doesn't look like an A plus.

00:09:02.103 --> 00:09:05.108
It doesn't look like 110 in extra credit.

00:09:05.108 --> 00:09:08.108
And failure isn't as simple as an F.

00:09:08.975 --> 00:09:13.208
And it's not always, like
failure can be very gray, right?

00:09:13.208 --> 00:09:16.842
And being able to discern
what you might arrive

00:09:16.842 --> 00:09:20.027
at an event in your life where you think

00:09:20.027 --> 00:09:22.310
that wow, I've succeeded.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:24.201
And you're getting the affirmation

00:09:24.201 --> 00:09:26.417
from all these outside forces.

00:09:26.417 --> 00:09:29.065
But if it's not aligned
authentically to who

00:09:29.065 --> 00:09:31.654
and what you are, it could
very much feel like failure.

00:09:31.654 --> 00:09:33.269
- You're going to fail.

00:09:33.269 --> 00:09:34.102
It's okay.

00:09:35.561 --> 00:09:36.394
Okay?

00:09:36.394 --> 00:09:37.688
You're going to fail.

00:09:37.688 --> 00:09:39.665
And I'm not talkin' about the tests.

00:09:39.665 --> 00:09:40.856
That's one thing.

00:09:40.856 --> 00:09:44.357
I'm talkin' about to your
knees, your skin bloody.

00:09:44.357 --> 00:09:45.721
Fail.

00:09:45.721 --> 00:09:47.566
And that's okay cause you know what?

00:09:47.566 --> 00:09:50.977
You know down deep inside of all of you,

00:09:50.977 --> 00:09:53.221
that's how you learn.

00:09:53.221 --> 00:09:55.079
You need to be motivated by failure.

00:09:55.079 --> 00:09:56.178
How'd you learn how to walk?

00:09:56.178 --> 00:09:58.782
You crawled, and you fell down.

00:09:58.782 --> 00:10:00.434
Busted your tooth.

00:10:00.434 --> 00:10:01.823
Got some blood in your mouth.

00:10:01.823 --> 00:10:03.630
Get up, and you walk.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:04.463
Right?

00:10:04.463 --> 00:10:06.119
Self-directed.

00:10:06.119 --> 00:10:08.369
- You should seek failures.

00:10:09.264 --> 00:10:13.221
See, if you're playing it
safe, you're not going to win.

00:10:13.221 --> 00:10:15.574
If you're playing it safe,

00:10:15.574 --> 00:10:17.476
like that old saying,
you know, you were taught

00:10:17.476 --> 00:10:18.598
when you were a little girl.

00:10:18.598 --> 00:10:19.758
Better to be safe than sorry.

00:10:19.758 --> 00:10:20.879
Well, that's a bunch of crap.

00:10:20.879 --> 00:10:24.046
It's not better to be safe than sorry.

00:10:24.977 --> 00:10:27.151
It's by trying things that you figure out

00:10:27.151 --> 00:10:29.567
how far you can go.

00:10:29.567 --> 00:10:32.243
You got to get outside the box.

00:10:32.243 --> 00:10:36.021
Like, it's reported
Edison tried 3,000 ways

00:10:36.021 --> 00:10:37.943
before he built the incandescent light.

00:10:37.943 --> 00:10:40.794
He said he didn't fail 3,000 times.

00:10:40.794 --> 00:10:42.995
He said there was 3,000 different steps

00:10:42.995 --> 00:10:45.078
to building a light bulb.

00:10:45.968 --> 00:10:49.001
Well, there's different steps
to get to where you're going.

00:10:49.001 --> 00:10:52.942
And I really do treat winning
and losing exactly the same.

00:10:52.942 --> 00:10:55.536
I do not let it upset me.

00:10:55.536 --> 00:10:56.777
- Do you think that's a big part

00:10:56.777 --> 00:10:59.052
of why you're so successful?

00:10:59.052 --> 00:11:02.411
- Well, it's part of why I enjoy it.

00:11:02.411 --> 00:11:05.714
Yeah, I think it is
cause I'll try anything.

00:11:05.714 --> 00:11:09.281
Like, if I'm into an
idea, the idea of losing

00:11:09.281 --> 00:11:11.626
never enters my mind.

00:11:11.626 --> 00:11:14.209
See, I have worked with giants.

00:11:15.966 --> 00:11:18.119
I had the good fortune of working

00:11:18.119 --> 00:11:20.771
with Sir Edmund Hillary.

00:11:20.771 --> 00:11:24.821
He was the first man to
stand on top of the world.

00:11:24.821 --> 00:11:29.265
And I worked with him on
three different occasions.

00:11:29.265 --> 00:11:32.272
And the only difference in
Ed Hillary and Bob Proctor

00:11:32.272 --> 00:11:33.954
is in his size.

00:11:33.954 --> 00:11:36.781
Now, he's gone now, but he was big man.

00:11:36.781 --> 00:11:38.440
When he shook hands with
me, his hand wrapped

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.846
right around mine.

00:11:39.846 --> 00:11:43.055
I felt like a dwarf, you know.

00:11:43.055 --> 00:11:47.041
And in talking to him,
it never entered his mind

00:11:47.041 --> 00:11:48.335
he wouldn't get to the
top of the mountain,

00:11:48.335 --> 00:11:50.123
but he failed in 1951.

00:11:50.123 --> 00:11:51.623
He failed in 1952.

00:11:53.174 --> 00:11:56.581
It wasn't until 1953 that he
got to the top of the mountain.

00:11:56.581 --> 00:12:00.520
You know, people had died for
centuries trying to do that.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:04.365
But he said, I knew if
I could see it in here,

00:12:04.365 --> 00:12:05.822
I could hold it out here.

00:12:05.822 --> 00:12:07.915
Stella Mann wrote that in a book.

00:12:07.915 --> 00:12:08.903
If you can see it in your head,

00:12:08.903 --> 00:12:10.649
you can hold it in your hand.

00:12:10.649 --> 00:12:11.919
And that's right.

00:12:11.919 --> 00:12:15.435
And if you're not prepared to
lose, you're never going to win.

00:12:15.435 --> 00:12:17.751
Cause you're always playing it safe,

00:12:17.751 --> 00:12:20.365
and there's no reward in that.

00:12:20.365 --> 00:12:21.539
- You know, I'm a woman in the business.

00:12:21.539 --> 00:12:22.372
- [Lori] That's right.

00:12:22.372 --> 00:12:23.608
- So are you, and it's
great because there are

00:12:23.608 --> 00:12:25.844
different personalities, successful.

00:12:25.844 --> 00:12:27.232
Be yourself.

00:12:27.232 --> 00:12:28.229
Take care of business.

00:12:28.229 --> 00:12:29.285
- Be yourself.

00:12:29.285 --> 00:12:30.118
- Go for it.

00:12:30.118 --> 00:12:30.951
- Yes.

00:12:30.951 --> 00:12:31.784
- Get out there.

00:12:31.784 --> 00:12:32.617
But it can be bumpy along the way.

00:12:32.617 --> 00:12:34.538
Any regrets or mistakes that you feel

00:12:34.538 --> 00:12:36.689
you've kind of hit through the years?

00:12:36.689 --> 00:12:38.806
- Well, you know, I share certain bumps

00:12:38.806 --> 00:12:40.408
that I've had in the book.

00:12:40.408 --> 00:12:42.483
I think that, you know, I
don't like to look back.

00:12:42.483 --> 00:12:43.843
There are no mistakes really.

00:12:43.843 --> 00:12:45.058
Everything is a learning lesson.

00:12:45.058 --> 00:12:46.715
Everything helps you to do better.

00:12:46.715 --> 00:12:47.548
- [Queen Latifah] Right.

00:12:47.548 --> 00:12:49.212
- I talk about some of
the mistakes that I made,

00:12:49.212 --> 00:12:52.010
and it just helps you
to get further along.

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.639
Learn from those
mistakes, and get smarter.

00:12:54.639 --> 00:12:56.648
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:56.648 --> 00:12:57.921
I hope you enjoyed.

00:12:57.921 --> 00:12:59.921
I'd love to know what was
your biggest take-away

00:12:59.921 --> 00:13:01.017
from this video?

00:13:01.017 --> 00:13:03.141
What are you going to immediately apply

00:13:03.141 --> 00:13:05.125
somehow to your life or to your business?

00:13:05.125 --> 00:13:06.832
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:13:06.832 --> 00:13:07.941
I'm super curious to find out.

00:13:07.941 --> 00:13:09.442
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:13:09.442 --> 00:13:12.315
to Wesley Lavinder from
fullyoptimized.org.

00:13:12.315 --> 00:13:13.993
Wesley, thank you so much for picking up

00:13:13.993 --> 00:13:15.759
a copy of my book Your One Word.

00:13:15.759 --> 00:13:17.485
It really, really means a lot to me,

00:13:17.485 --> 00:13:19.233
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:13:19.233 --> 00:13:20.686
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:20.686 --> 00:13:21.684
I believe in you.

00:13:21.684 --> 00:13:23.836
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:13:23.836 --> 00:13:27.194
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:13:27.194 --> 00:13:28.089
I'll see you soon.

00:13:28.089 --> 00:13:30.339
(swooshes)

